RI(9)/VEDIT Family - Printing/
M(H)			!Display header

Q23YEA			!Use highlight attribute
YEN YT/			      --- WARNING !!! ---/ YEN
Q27YEA			!Restore attribute

YT/
Do not run this part of the demo if you do not have a printer connected!!

You can print the entire file being edited or just a portion of it.  Printing
is normally 60 lines per page with a 10 column (1 inch) left margin and
without a header or page numbers.

VEDIT and VEDIT PLUS are supplied with the print "macro" PRINT.VDM which can
be used to print an entire file with a header on each page.  The header
consists of the file name, the date and the page number.

	--- Press <Esc> if you do not have a printer connected ---

	--- OR  Press <Enter> to continue ---
/

XK(0)//
(Q0 = 27) [ RJ(Z) ]	!Back to main menu if <Esc> was pressed

9XS(100)		!Need 9 line window
M(W)			!Create instruction window; set attributes
EZY			!Empty main edit buffer
EB demo.txt		!Load demo text

EE(1)			!Switch to instruction buffer
B#K			!Clear old contents
I/To print press <Alt-P> for the {PRINT} sub-menu.  To print the entire file
press "A" to select "All".

You can stop the printing before it is done by pressing <Ctrl-C>.

When necessary, you can advance the printer to the top of the next page by
pressing <Alt-P> and then "E" to select "Eject".  This is also a convenient
way of sending a blank page through the printer.
		--- Press <Esc> to continue ---/

B -V			!Display instructions
EE(@)			!Back to main text
V

EE(1)
B#K
I/To print a portion of the file, move the cursor to the FIRST character to be
printed.  Then press <F9> to set the 1st marker and begin highlighting.
Next, move the cursor one position PAST the LAST character to be printed.
(Generally, this will be the beginning of the next line.)  Press <Alt-P> and
"B" again (or press the "hot-key" <Ctrl-P> which directly accesses the {PRINT,
Block} function).  The text will start printing.

You may want to press <Alt-P> and "E" to advance the printer to the top of
the next page.		--- Press <Esc> to continue ---/

B -V
EE(@)
V

+RL(p) print.vdm		!Load the print macro

EE(1)
B#K
I/This demo has loaded the print "macro" PRINT.VDM for you.  The following
steps let you print the entire file using this macro.

Press <Alt-M> for the {MISC} sub-menu.  Select "Execute Macro".  At the
prompt press "P".  The file should begin printing.

Notice how the printed pages now have the file name, date and page number at
the top.
		--- Press <Esc> to return to the Main Menu ---/

B -V
EE(@)
V

EZY
RE(P)
